  {
    "id": "ishikawa-e2e-12-should-render-correctly-when-effect-is-indented-more-than-causes",
    "origin": "e2e/diagrams/ishikawa/pr-check/12-should-render-correctly-when-effect-is-indented-more-than-causes.mmd",
    "source": "---\ndescription: >-\n  Edge case where the effect (Problem) and every cause/sub-cause line share\n  the same two-space indentation, so none of the \"Subcause\" items are\n  indented deeper than their intended parent. Verifies the parser still\n  identifies the first line as the effect and renders the rest as flat\n  top-level causes when indentation alone doesn't encode a hierarchy.\n---\nishikawa-beta\n  Problem\n  Cause A\n  Subcause A1\n  Subcause A2\n  Cause B\n  Subcause B1\n  Cause C\n",
    "expect": {
      "roots": [
        {
          "label": "Problem",
          "children": [
            {
              "label": "Cause A",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "label": "Subcause A1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "label": "Subcause A2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "label": "Cause B",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "label": "Subcause B1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "label": "Cause C",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "title": "",
      "accessibilityTitle": "",
      "accessibilityDescription": ""
    }
